<title>NORWAY: FORECAST-Storebrand Q1 profits seen up.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Storebrand Q1 profits seen up.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Storebrand ASA, Norway's biggest insurance company, is expected to post first-quarter group results of 288 million crowns, up from 246 million in the corresponding 1996 period, according to a consensus forecast by seven analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>Three recommended to buy the share, two said hold and two said sell.</p>
<p>All analysts said they expected the proposed merger between Storebrand and Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse to come about. A merger between the two would form the biggest financial institution in the country.</p>
<p>Storebrand will present the first-quarter result at 0730 GMT on Tuesday.</p>
<p>					  Three months to March 31</p>
<p>				    (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
